# Descartes, Discourse on Method, opening
atom	content	everyone thinks himself abundantly provided with good sense and desires no larger measure of it
atom	not_all_mistaken	not all are mistaken in this conviction
atom	reason_equal	good sense or reason, the power of judging aright and distinguishing truth from error, is by nature equal in all men (good sense is the most equally distributed thing)
atom	diversity_from_reason	the diversity of our opinions arises from some being endowed with a larger share of reason than others
atom	diversity_from_conduct	the diversity of our opinions arises from our conducting our thoughts along different ways and not fixing attention on the same objects
atom	application_decisive	to possess a vigorous mind is not enough; the prime requisite is rightly to apply it
P1	S1	content	kind empirical
P2	S2	not_all_mistaken
P3	S2	content ∧ not_all_mistaken → reason_equal
C1	S2	reason_equal	from P1 P2 P3
P4	S2	reason_equal → ¬diversity_from_reason
P5	S3	application_decisive
# the text assumes these are the only two candidate sources of diverse opinions
A1	-	diversity_from_reason ∨ diversity_from_conduct
